IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 5 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 5 (PENAL PROVISIONS, ss 38 to 41) and PART 5A (PROVISIONS RELATING TO
-- COURT PROCEEDINGS, ss 41A to 41E).
-- Policy for "unless the contrary intention appears": a plain yes/no input, NOTHING when it is TRUE.

§ `Section 38 -- attempt to commit an offence to be deemed an offence`

-- src:1624 | 38. A provision which constitutes an offence is, unless the contrary
-- src:1625 | intention appears, deemed to provide also that an attempt to commit
-- src:1626 | that offence shall be an offence against the provision, punishable as if
-- src:1627 | the offence itself had been committed.
@ref s 38 (src:1624-1627)
GIVEN `a provision constitutes an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an attempt to commit the offence is an offence against the provision, punishable as if the offence itself had been committed` `a provision constitutes an offence` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a provision constitutes an offence` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 39 -- imposition of penalty not a bar to civil action`

-- src:1634 | 39. The imposition of a penalty by any written law, in the absence
-- src:1635 | of express provision to the contrary, does not relieve any person from
-- src:1636 | liability to answer for damages to a person injured.
@ref s 39 (src:1634-1636)
GIVEN `a penalty is imposed by a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is express provision to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the penalty relieves the person from liability to answer for damages to a person injured` `a penalty is imposed by a written law` `there is express provision to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `a penalty is imposed by a written law` AND (NOT `there is express provision to the contrary`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 40 -- provisions as to offences under 2 or more laws`

-- src:1640 | 40. Where any act or omission constitutes an offence under 2 or
-- src:1641 | more written laws, the offender shall, unless the contrary intention
-- src:1642 | appears, be liable to be prosecuted and punished under any one of
-- src:1643 | those written laws but shall not be liable to be punished twice for the
-- src:1644 | same offence.
@ref s 40 (src:1640-1644)
GIVEN `the number of written laws under which the act or omission is an offence` IS A NUMBER
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under any one of those written laws` `the number of written laws under which the act or omission is an offence` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the number of written laws under which the act or omission is an offence` AT LEAST 2 AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 40 but not liable to be punished twice for the same offence (src:1642-1644)
GIVEN `the number of written laws under which the act or omission is an offence` IS A NUMBER
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same offence` `the number of written laws under which the act or omission is an offence` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the number of written laws under which the act or omission is an offence` AT LEAST 2 AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 41 -- penalties prescribed to be deemed maximum penalties`

-- src:1648 | 41. Whenever in any written law a penalty is provided for an
-- src:1649 | offence, such provision implies that the offence shall be punishable
-- src:1650 | upon conviction by a penalty not exceeding (except as may be
-- src:1651 | otherwise expressly mentioned in the written law) the penalty
-- src:1652 | provided.
@ref s 41 (src:1648-1652)
GIVEN `the penalty provided for the offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the written law expressly mentions otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most the offence is punishable by on conviction` `the penalty provided for the offence` `the written law expressly mentions otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the written law expressly mentions otherwise` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the penalty provided for the offence`

@ref s 41 a penalty not exceeding the penalty provided (src:1650-1652)
GIVEN `the penalty imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalty provided for the offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the written law expressly mentions otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the penalty imposed is within what section 41 allows` `the penalty imposed` `the penalty provided for the offence` `the written law expressly mentions otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the written law expressly mentions otherwise` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (`the penalty imposed` AT MOST `the penalty provided for the offence`)

§ `Section 41A -- process for making applications to Court in civil proceedings`

DECLARE `Process of an application` IS ONE OF
    `an originating application`
    `a summons`

-- src:1660 | 41A.—(1) Where any written law that provides for an application
-- src:1661 | in any civil proceedings to be made to a Court —
-- src:1663 | (a) does not prescribe the process by which the application is
-- src:1664 | to be made; or
-- src:1666 | (b) prescribes that the application is to be made by way of a
-- src:1667 | petition, a motion, an originating motion or a summons in
-- src:1668 | chambers,
-- src:1670 | that written law is, in relation to any such application that is made
-- src:1671 | thereunder on or after 1 April 2022, deemed to require that the
-- src:1672 | application must be made —
-- src:1677 | (c) by way of an originating application, if it commences the
-- src:1678 | proceedings; or
-- src:1680 | [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:1682 | (d) by way of a summons, if it is made in proceedings that are
-- src:1683 | pending.
-- src:1685 | [42/2005]
-- src:1687 | [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:1689 | [Act 19 of 2025 wef 05/12/2025]
-- src:1716 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to —
-- src:1718 | (a) petitions of appeal; or
-- src:1720 | (b) such other class or classes of applications to or proceedings
-- src:1721 | in the Court as may be prescribed under subsection (7).
-- src:1723 | [42/2005]
@ref s 41A(1), (3) (src:1660-1723)
GIVEN `a written law provides for an application in civil proceedings to be made to a Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the written law prescribes no process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written law prescribes a petition, a motion, an originating motion or a summons in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it commences the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in proceedings that are pending` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a petition of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a class prescribed under section 41A(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Process of an application`
`the process the application must be made by` `a written law provides for an application in civil proceedings to be made to a Court` `the day the application is made` `the written law prescribes no process` `the written law prescribes a petition, a motion, an originating motion or a summons in chambers` `it commences the proceedings` `it is made in proceedings that are pending` `it is a petition of appeal` `it is in a class prescribed under section 41A(7)` MEANS
    IF `a written law provides for an application in civil proceedings to be made to a Court`
       AND `the day the application is made` AT LEAST Date 1 4 2022
       AND (`the written law prescribes no process` OR `the written law prescribes a petition, a motion, an originating motion or a summons in chambers`)
       AND (NOT `it is a petition of appeal`)
       AND (NOT `it is in a class prescribed under section 41A(7)`)
    THEN BRANCH
             IF `it commences the proceedings` THEN JUST `an originating application`
             IF `it is made in proceedings that are pending` THEN JUST `a summons`
             OTHERWISE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1691 | (2) Where pursuant to subsection (1) an application is made to a
-- src:1692 | Court under any written law by way of an originating application or a
-- src:1693 | summons —
-- src:1695 | (a) the application must be made in accordance with the Rules
-- src:1696 | of Court;
-- src:1698 | (b) the Court may give to the parties to the application any
-- src:1699 | directions that the Court thinks just and expedient for the
-- src:1700 | purpose of facilitating the progress of the application as an
-- src:1701 | application made by originating application or summons,
-- src:1702 | as the case may be; and
-- src:1704 | [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:1706 | (c) any provision in that written law that relates to the practice
-- src:1707 | and procedure for making such an application and which is
-- src:1708 | inconsistent with this section or with the Rules of Court
-- src:1709 | has, to the extent of the inconsistency, no effect in relation
-- src:1710 | to that application.
-- src:1712 | [42/2005]
-- src:1714 | [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref s 41A(2) (src:1691-1714)
GIVEN `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of the written law on practice and procedure is inconsistent with section 41A or the Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`that provision has any effect in relation to the application` `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` `a provision of the written law on practice and procedure is inconsistent with section 41A or the Rules of Court` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` AND `a provision of the written law on practice and procedure is inconsistent with section 41A or the Rules of Court`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 41A(2)(a) in accordance with the Rules of Court (src:1695-1696)
GIVEN `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the application must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court` `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 41A(2)(b) directions (src:1698-1702)
GIVEN `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Court may give the parties directions the Court thinks just and expedient to facilitate the progress of the application` `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by originating application or summons under section 41A(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1725 | (4) Nothing in this section prevents any relief obtainable by way of
-- src:1726 | an application to a Court under any written law from being included
-- src:1731 | as one of the reliefs sought in an originating claim by which an action
-- src:1732 | is commenced before the Court.
@ref s 41A(4) (src:1725-1732)
GIVEN `the relief is obtainable by way of an application to a Court under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 41A prevents the relief being included among the reliefs sought in an originating claim` `the relief is obtainable by way of an application to a Court under a written law` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:1738 | (5) To avoid doubt, any application that —
-- src:1740 | (a) was made to a Court before 1 April 2022 under any written
-- src:1741 | law to which subsection (1) applies; and
-- src:1743 | [Act 19 of 2025 wef 05/12/2025]
-- src:1745 | (b) is pending before the Court on or after that date,
-- src:1747 | continues, unless otherwise ordered by the Court, to proceed in
-- src:1748 | accordance with the provisions of the relevant written law and the
-- src:1749 | practice and procedure as were in force and applicable in relation to
-- src:1750 | that application immediately before that date, until the application is
-- src:1751 | finally disposed of by the Court.
@ref s 41A(5) (src:1738-1751)
GIVEN `section 41A(1) applies to the written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
      `it is pending on or after 1 April 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the application continues under the practice and procedure in force immediately before 1 April 2022` `section 41A(1) applies to the written law` `the day the application was made` `it is pending on or after 1 April 2022` `the Court orders otherwise` MEANS
    IF `section 41A(1) applies to the written law` AND `the day the application was made` BELOW Date 1 4 2022 AND `it is pending on or after 1 April 2022`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the Court orders otherwise`)
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `A court` IS ONE OF
    `the Court of Appeal or a judge sitting in that Court`
    `the Appellate Division of the High Court or a judge sitting in that Division`
    `the General Division of the High Court or a judge sitting in that Division`
    `a District Court`
    `a Magistrate's Court`
    `another court prescribed under section 41A(7)`
    `some other court`

-- src:1755 | (6) In this section, “Court” means —
-- src:1757 | (a) the Court of Appeal or a judge sitting in that Court;
-- src:1759 | (b) the Appellate Division of the High Court or a judge sitting
-- src:1760 | in that Division;
-- src:1762 | (ba) the General Division of the High Court or a judge sitting in
-- src:1763 | that Division;
-- src:1765 | (c) a District Court;
-- src:1767 | (d) a Magistrate’s Court; and
-- src:1769 | (e) such other court as may be prescribed.
-- src:1771 | [42/2005; 42/2014; 40/2019]
@ref s 41A(6) (src:1755-1771)
GIVEN `the court` IS A `A court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a Court for section 41A` `the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court`
    WHEN `some other court` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 41B -- renaming of prerogative orders or writs`

-- A row of a table of s 41B, 41D or 41E: the old expression and the new one.
DECLARE `Reference row` HAS
    paragraph IS A STRING
    `first column` IS A STRING
    `second column` IS A STRING

-- src:1796 | (a) mandamus Mandatory Order
@ref s 41B(a) (src:1796-1796)
`s 41B (a)` MEANS
    `Reference row` OF "(a)", "mandamus", "Mandatory Order"

-- src:1797 | (b) certiorari Quashing Order
@ref s 41B(b) (src:1797-1797)
`s 41B (b)` MEANS
    `Reference row` OF "(b)", "certiorari", "Quashing Order"

-- src:1799 | (c) prohibition Prohibiting Order
@ref s 41B(c) (src:1799-1799)
`s 41B (c)` MEANS
    `Reference row` OF "(c)", "prohibition", "Prohibiting Order"

-- src:1801 | (d) writ of habeas corpus Order for Review of Detention.
@ref s 41B(d) (src:1801-1801)
`s 41B (d)` MEANS
    `Reference row` OF "(d)", "writ of habeas corpus", "Order for Review of Detention"

-- src:1788 | 41B. As from 1 January 2006, the prerogative orders or writs
-- src:1789 | issuable by the High Court as listed in the first column below are to be
-- src:1790 | referred to by the corresponding expressions as set out in the
-- src:1791 | second column and, in all written laws, the expressions as set out in
-- src:1792 | the second column are to be construed accordingly:
-- src:1794 | First column . Second column
@ref s 41B chapeau (src:1788-1794)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Reference row`
`the table of section 41B` MEANS
    LIST `s 41B (a)`, `s 41B (b)`, `s 41B (c)`, `s 41B (d)`

@ref s 41B as from 1 January 2006 (src:1788-1794)
GIVEN `the expression` IS A STRING
      `the day it is read` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` `the expression` `the day it is read` MEANS
    IF `the day it is read` AT LEAST Date 1 1 2006
    THEN CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD row's `first column` EQUALS `the expression`) `the table of section 41B`
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
         WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (row's `second column`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 41C -- references to High Court before 2 January 2021`

DECLARE `What the reference to the High Court is about` IS ONE OF
    `a provision conferring jurisdiction or power on the High Court`
    `an appeal or other process to or from the High Court`
    `a power to make subsidiary legislation in relation to proceedings in the High Court`

-- src:1807 | 41C. In any written law enacted or made before 2 January 2021 —
-- src:1809 | (a) a provision that confers any jurisdiction or power on the
-- src:1810 | High Court is, on or after that date, to be read as conferring
-- src:1811 | that jurisdiction or power on the General Division of the
-- src:1812 | High Court;
-- src:1814 | (b) a reference to an appeal or other process to or from the
-- src:1815 | High Court is, on or after that date, to be read as a reference
-- src:1816 | to an appeal to or from the General Division of the High
-- src:1817 | Court; and
-- src:1819 | (c) a power to make subsidiary legislation in relation to
-- src:1820 | proceedings in the High Court is, on or after that date, to be
-- src:1821 | read as a power to make subsidiary legislation in relation to
-- src:1822 | proceedings in both the General Division of the High Court
-- src:1823 | and Appellate Division of the High Court.
@ref s 41C (src:1807-1823)
GIVEN `the written law was enacted or made on` IS A DATE
      `the day it is read` IS A DATE
      `the reference is about` IS A `What the reference to the High Court is about`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the reference to the High Court is read as` `the written law was enacted or made on` `the day it is read` `the reference is about` MEANS
    IF `the written law was enacted or made on` BELOW Date 2 1 2021 AND `the day it is read` AT LEAST Date 2 1 2021
    THEN CONSIDER `the reference is about`
         WHEN `a provision conferring jurisdiction or power on the High Court` THEN JUST "conferring that jurisdiction or power on the General Division of the High Court"
         WHEN `an appeal or other process to or from the High Court` THEN JUST "an appeal to or from the General Division of the High Court"
         WHEN `a power to make subsidiary legislation in relation to proceedings in the High Court` THEN JUST "a power to make subsidiary legislation in relation to proceedings in both the General Division of the High Court and Appellate Division of the High Court"
    ELSE NOTHING

